  "resume": "=== Bianka Pena - Resume.pdf ===\nBIANKA NICOLLE PENA MARCELINO\n\nTemple, PA 19560\n\n6469721673 - bianka.pena.marcelino@gmail.com\n\nWEBSITES, PORTFOLIOS, PROFILES\n\n•\n\nlinkedin.com/in/bianka-pena-708173232\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\nDedicated Psychology and Biology student with a passion for understanding the complexities\n\nof  human behavior, health, and the factors that influence lives. Extensive experience in HIV\n\nresearch, clinical care, and public health has fostered a strong commitment to making a\n\nmeaningful impact in underserved communities. Eager to further develop research skills and\n\ncontribute to advancements in epidemiology, focusing on addressing health disparities and\n\npromoting wellness. Proactive learner driven by a desire to translate academic knowledge into\n\npractical solutions that enhance community health outcomes.\n\nSKILLS\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\nClient advocacy\n\nRelationship building\n\nStrategic planning\n\nTime management\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\nTeamwork\n\nConflict resolution\n\nReport writing\n\nAnalytical thinking\n\nRESEARCH & CLINICAL EXPERIENCE\n05/2025 to 05/2026\nCounselor Aide\n\nHelio Health – Syracuse, NY\n\n•\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n\nProvided direct resident care in substance use disorder treatment settings.\n\nAdministered medications as a med-certified aide and maintained HIPAA-compliant\n\ndocumentation.\n\nMonitored resident behavior and medication effects, reporting concerns to clinical staff.\n\nSupported daily routines, crisis de-escalation, and recovery goals across varied shifts.\n\nHere are six original resume statements that reflect high-value responsibilities for the\n\nCounselor's Aide role at Helio Health, filling gaps in the existing work history while\n\nmaintaining the user's writing style:\n\n09/2024 to 05/2026\n\nPeer Academic Leader (PAL)\n\nLe Moyne College – Syracuse, NY\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n\nFacilitated structured study halls supporting undergraduate academic success.\n\nCoached students on time management, study strategies, and accountability.\n\nMonitored attendance and engagement while maintaining supportive peer relationships.\n\nMentored students and connected them with campus academic resources.\n\nDeveloped and implemented engaging academic workshops to enhance student study\n\nskills.\n\nCoordinated with faculty to align tutoring sessions with course objectives and\n\nrequirements.\n\n\f06/2024 to 05/2026\n\nResearch Student\n\nLe Moyne College – Syracuse, NY\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\n•\n\nConducted HIV-1 research on pathogenesis and host restriction factors.\n\nPerformed cell culture (THP-1), DNA extraction, SDS-PAGE, and Western blotting.\n\nTrained and mentored new lab members in research techniques and lab protocols.\n\nAssisted with experimental design, data analysis, and research presentations.\n\nAssisted in laboratory maintenance, ensuring equipment and supplies were properly\n\norganized.\n\nCollaborated with team members to refine research protocols and improve efficiency.\n\n06/2023 to 08/2023\n\nSummer Research Intern\n\nUASD – Santo Domingo, Dominican Republic\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\nContributed to a public health research project on maternal mortality and healthcare\n\naccess.\n\nAssisted with data collection, organization, and review of  maternal health indicators.\n\nAnalyzed social, economic, and healthcare system factors affecting maternal outcomes.\n\nSupported research discussions and summarized key findings.\n\nAssisted in the preparation of  research proposals and grant applications for funding.\n\nConducted literature reviews to identify relevant studies and inform research\n\nmethodologies.\n\nBachelor of  Science: Psychology\n\nLe Moyne - Syracuse, NY\n\nBachelor of  Arts: Biology\n\nLe Moyne - Syracuse, NY\n\nEDUCATION\n\n05/2026 \n\n05/2026 \n\nCERTIFICATIONS\n\n•\n•\n\nImproving Global Health: Focusing on Quality and Safety\n\nCPR / AED\n\nCOMMUNITY SERVICE & VOLUNTEER WORK\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n\nWescott Community